---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ScenarioPlayer from '../components/ScenarioPlayer.astro';
import CodeTabs from '../components/CodeTabs.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Hop, the network that finds a way"
  description="Hop is a delay-tolerant mesh: end-to-end encrypted datagrams that hop device to device, over BLE, Wi-Fi, and the internet, until they reach the person or service you meant. Held until they land or expire, not dropped for a missing network. One transport every offline app builds on."
  path="/"
>
  <!-- hero: the scenario player is the pitch -->
  <section class="hero" style="padding-bottom:28px;">
    <div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:14px;">Delay-tolerant mesh transport</div>
      <h1 style="max-width:none;margin:0 auto;">The network that finds a way.</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin:20px auto 0;">
        Encrypted datagrams hop device to device, over BLE, Wi-Fi, and the internet, until they
        reach the person or service you meant. No tower required. Held until they land or expire,
        not dropped for a missing network.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta" style="justify-content:center;">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://dashboard.hopme.sh/">Start free →</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/protocol/">Read the protocol</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-bottom:clamp(40px,6vw,72px);">
    <div class="wrap">
      <ScenarioPlayer ids={['disaster','event','mine','offgrid','expedition','ski','clockin','lora']} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- full-bleed value band -->
  <section class="fullband">
    <img src="/band-hero.jpg" alt="A dark valley at night, a distant town glowing, scattered figures carrying faint signal across the expanse" width="1920" height="823" loading="lazy" />
    <div class="fullband-ov">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="eyebrow">Delay-tolerant by design</div>
        <h2>When the path disappears, the message keeps moving.</h2>
        <p>Held on the devices around you, re-offered at every encounter, delivered the moment a
           way opens. No tower. No server required.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- the narrow waist / build on Hop -->
  <section class="band band-soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Why one protocol covers all of it</div>
        <h2>One layer. Every offline app.</h2>
        <p>Disaster, off-grid sensors, a region cut off, a phone with no plan, same problem: no
           reliable path, right now. Most offline products rebuild that transport and weld it to a
           single app. Hop is that layer, done once, a sealed, store-and-forward datagram. The
           narrow waist for intermittent networks: many apps above, many bearers below. The core
           only moves bytes, a thin per-platform driver runs the radios.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="layerstack">
        <div class="lrow">
          <span class="lvl">Apps</span>
          <div class="chips">
            <a class="lchip" href="/use-cases/messaging/">Messaging</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/use-cases/sync/">Data sync</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/use-cases/files/">File transfer</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/use-cases/web/">Offline web</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/use-cases/telemetry/">Telemetry</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/use-cases/broadcast/">Alerts</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lrow">
          <span class="lvl">Semantics</span>
          <div class="chips">
            <a class="lchip code" href="/protocol/hops/">hops://</a>
            <a class="lchip code" href="/protocol/hps/">hps://</a>
            <a class="lchip code" href="/protocol/streams/">streams</a>
            <a class="lchip code" href="/protocol/hns/">HNS</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lrow waist">
          <span class="lvl">Waist</span>
          <div class="chips">
            <a class="lchip code" href="/protocol/hdp/">hdp://</a>
            <span class="lchip">end-to-end encrypted, store-and-forward datagrams</span>
          </div>
          <span class="waisttag">the waist</span>
        </div>
        <div class="lrow bearer">
          <span class="lvl">Bearer</span>
          <div class="chips">
            <a class="lchip" href="/protocol/ble/">BLE</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/protocol/l2cap/">Direct channel</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/protocol/tcp/">Internet relay</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/protocol/bearers/">Wi-Fi · any transport…</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lrow driver">
          <span class="lvl">Driver</span>
          <div class="chips">
            <a class="lchip" href="/docs/drivers/ios/">iOS</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/docs/drivers/android/">Android</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/docs/drivers/macos/">macOS</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/docs/drivers/esp32/">ESP32</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/docs/drivers/linux/">Linux · server</a>
            <a class="lchip" href="/docs/">your platform…</a>
          </div>
          <span class="waisttag">drives the radios</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- where Hop runs (imagery) -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Where Hop runs</div>
        <h2>Where the network can't be assumed.</h2>
        <p>The same fabric, wherever coordination outruns connectivity.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenes">
        <a class="scene" href="/business/">
          <img src="/scene-events.jpg" alt="A dense night-festival crowd, a sea of glowing phones" width="1280" height="853" loading="lazy" />
          <div class="ov"><div class="k">Events &amp; venues</div><h3>When 50,000 phones crush the tower.</h3><p>Relay peer to peer instead of fighting for a cell.</p></div>
        </a>
        <a class="scene" href="/public-safety-defense/">
          <img src="/scene-response.jpg" alt="Search-and-rescue responders coordinating on a tablet, dark city skyline" width="1280" height="853" loading="lazy" />
          <div class="ov"><div class="k">Response &amp; defense</div><h3>Coordination when the grid goes down.</h3><p>No tower, no server, the people on scene are the network.</p></div>
        </a>
        <a class="scene" href="/business/">
          <img src="/scene-expedition.jpg" alt="Hikers on a high mountain ridgeline, far from coverage" width="1280" height="853" loading="lazy" />
          <div class="ov"><div class="k">Expedition &amp; remote</div><h3>Past the last bar of signal.</h3><p>Messages hop person to person until they reach the group.</p></div>
        </a>
        <a class="scene" href="/lora/">
          <img src="/scene-maritime.jpg" alt="A marina and dark sea at dusk with a distant shoreline" width="1280" height="853" loading="lazy" />
          <div class="ov"><div class="k">Maritime &amp; rural</div><h3>Distance a phone can't cross.</h3><p>A long-range 900 MHz bridge stretches the mesh across the gap.</p></div>
        </a>
        <a class="scene" href="/business/">
          <img src="/scene-agriculture.jpg" alt="A vast farm, crop rows to the horizon, a worker far across the field" width="1280" height="853" loading="lazy" />
          <div class="ov"><div class="k">Agriculture &amp; land</div><h3>Operations spread across kilometres.</h3><p>Sensors, vehicles, and crews stay in sync past Wi-Fi's edge.</p></div>
        </a>
        <a class="scene" href="/business/">
          <img src="/scene-industrial.jpg" alt="A container yard or mine site at dusk with scattered work-lights" width="1280" height="853" loading="lazy" />
          <div class="ov"><div class="k">Industrial &amp; sites</div><h3>Yards, mines, sites with no coverage.</h3><p>Crews and equipment relay through each other across the site.</p></div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- drop it into your app (code toggle) -->
  <section class="band band-soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid-2" style="align-items:center; gap:44px;">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Drop it into your app</div>
          <h2>One core. iOS, Android, Rust.</h2>
          <p class="lede">A pure-Rust core with native bindings via UniFFI. Open a node from a key,
             address a sealed payload, drain your inbox, the mesh handles relaying, custody, and delivery.</p>
          <div class="hero-cta">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs/quickstart/">Quickstart →</a>
            <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/developers/">For developers</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div><CodeTabs /></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- how it's monetized -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">The model</div>
        <h2>The library is free. The cloud is the product.</h2>
        <p class="lede">The device does the work, so the SDK is open and free. The cloud backbone
           costs money to run, so that's what you pay for, only when you use it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="layers">
        <div class="layer">
          <div class="lv">Layer 0</div>
          <h3>Open SDK</h3>
          <p>Embed <code>hop-core</code> on iOS &amp; Android. Source-available, free forever.</p>
          <div class="who">Free</div>
        </div>
        <div class="layer paid">
          <div class="lv">Layer 1</div>
          <h3>Hosted backbone</h3>
          <p>Managed relay fleet, durable mailboxes, internet egress, <code>hops://</code> endpoints.</p>
          <div class="who">Usage-based</div>
        </div>
        <div class="layer">
          <div class="lv">Layer 2</div>
          <h3>Commercial license</h3>
          <p>Terms beyond the FSL non-compete, for products that need them.</p>
          <div class="who">Enterprise</div>
        </div>
        <div class="layer">
          <div class="lv">Layer 3</div>
          <h3>Private &amp; mission</h3>
          <p>On-prem fleets, private backbones, and support for field operations.</p>
          <div class="who">Solutions</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- cta -->
  <section class="cta-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Build for where the network goes dark.</h2>
      <p>Embed the free SDK today. Add the cloud backbone when you need to reach across the world.</p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://dashboard.hopme.sh/">Start free →</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/pricing/">See pricing</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
